# The binary Golay code, the [24,12,8] code that builds the Leech lattice and carries the Mathieu group. It packs twelve
# information bits into twenty-four, so it holds two to the twelfth, four thousand ninety-six, codewords, and any two
# differ in at least eight places, so it corrects any three errors. Its weight enumerator is symmetric and exact: one word
# of weight zero, seven hundred fifty-nine words of weight eight, two thousand five hundred seventy-six of weight twelve,
# seven hundred fifty-nine of weight sixteen, and one of weight twenty-four, summing to four thousand ninety-six. The seven
# hundred fifty-nine weight-eight words are the OCTADS, and they form a Steiner system: every five of the twenty-four
# coordinates lie in exactly one octad, so the octad count is twenty-four choose five divided by eight choose five, forty-
# two thousand five hundred four over fifty-six, seven hundred fifty-nine. Those same octads build the second shell of the
# Leech lattice, one hundred twenty-eight times seven hundred fifty-nine, and the code's automorphism group is the Mathieu
# group on twenty-four points. This file checks the codeword count, the symmetric weight enumerator, the Steiner octad
# count, and the Leech octad shell.

# The Golay code has 2^12 = 4096 codewords, which is sixty-four squared, 64 * 64 = 4096, and sixty-four is two to the
# sixth.
hold golay-has-four-thousand-ninety-six-codewords
  call is-equal
    code 4096
    call multiply
      code 64
      code 64

# The symmetric weight enumerator sums to the full codeword count: 1 + 759 + 2576 + 759 + 1 = 4096.
hold golay-weight-enumerator-sums-to-four-thousand-ninety-six
  call is-equal
    code 4096
    call add
      code 1
      call add
        code 759
        call add
          code 2576
          call add
            code 759
            code 1

# The octads form a Steiner system S(5,8,24): every 5 points lie in exactly one octad, so 759 * 56 = 42504 = (24 choose 5),
# with 56 the (8 choose 5) count of five-subsets inside one octad.
hold octads-form-a-steiner-system
  call is-equal
    call multiply
      code 759
      code 56
    code 42504

# The 759 octads build the second Leech shell with signed coordinates: 128 * 759 = 97152, one of the three shapes whose
# sum is the Leech kissing number.
hold octads-build-the-leech-octad-shell
  call is-equal
    code 97152
    call multiply
      code 128
      code 759

# Minimum distance eight corrects any three errors: the correctable-error radius is the distance minus one over two,
# (8 - 2) / 2 = 3, written as 3 * 2 = 8 - 2.
hold golay-corrects-three-errors
  call is-equal
    call multiply
      code 3
      code 2
    call subtract
      code 8
      code 2
